T1 (hand proof re-checked by inspection): c=a(1); if pi(2v-c)<pi(v) for all v>=2c+1 the orbit v_{k+1}=2v_k-c stays in [2c+1,inf) (2v-c>=3c+2>=2c+1 for c>=1) and gives an infinite strictly pi-decreasing sequence -- impossible in a type-omega order. VALID.
T2 (hand proof re-checked): x:=c-d=2c-v <= -1 <= 0 for v>=2c+1, so x sits at a position < s, before all of the right part; (c-d,c,c+d,c+2d) is then an increasing monotone 4-AP. VALID (given T1's descent applied inside the right part, whose value set is N minus a finite set -- the orbit-avoidance count is correct: g^k(v)=f forces v=c+(f-c)/2^k).
